     "text": "Weaver-Washington Clinic\nRe: Joseph Hernandez (DOB 01/19/1983)\n\n---\n\nDr. Smith\n\nJune 11, 2026: Joseph Hernandez, a 43-year-old male, presented today for follow-up regarding his heart failure and cardiomyopathy. His current medications include 12.5 mg and empagliflozin 10 mg. During this visit, his blood pressure was recorded at 139/90, and his weight was 122 pounds. He continues to have heart failure and cardiomyopathy, with an ejection fraction (EF) of 38%. This condition has been under control for approximately one year now. His current status is stable, and there are no new issues.\n\nOctober 15, 2025: Joseph was seen again on this date for his heart failure and cardiomyopathy. His blood pressure was 136/88, and his weight was 119 pounds. He remains stable and doing well. His medications, carvedilol 12.5 mg and empagliflozin 10 mg, are being continued. The patient reports no new symptoms and heart failure and cardiomyopathy are well-managed.\n\nFebruary 17, 2025: Joseph's follow-up visit on this date also centered on his heart failure and cardiomyopathy. At that time, his blood pressure was 140/91, and he weighed 125 pounds. He continues to do well without any new issues. The EF remains at 38%. His medications, carvedilol 12.5 mg and empagliflozin 10 mg, are maintained. The patient reports no additional symptoms and his heart condition remains stable.\n\nJune 22, 2024: Joseph's initial visit on this date was to address his heart failure and cardiomyopathy. His blood pressure that time was 140/81, and he weighed 124 pounds. We diagnosed him with heart failure and cardiomyopathy, with an EF of 38%. This condition had been ongoing, and it was noted that he had been recovering for about one year. His current medications include carvedilol 12.5 mg and empagliflozin 10 mg, which are helping to manage his condition effectively.\n\nSocial History: Joseph is a former smoker who quit in April 2025 after smoking half a pack per day starting in March 2009. His current alcohol consumption is approximately six drinks per week. His mother had hypertension and passed away at the age of 75. \n\n---\n\nDr. Dylan Gonzalez\nWeaver-Washington Clinic\nCardiology\n\n[End of Document]\n"
